Released under Apache 2.0 license as described in the file LICENSE.

# L4 — family-level uniform covering bounds from uniform doubling

Round-3 of the L4 geometric critical path proves the *pair-level* theorem
`Poincare.L4.Compactness.coveringNumber_univ_le_of_ghDist_lt_of_doubling`
(`release/Poincare/L4/Compactness/DoublingToCovers.lean`): if `X` is
Gromov–Hausdorff close to a doubling space `Y` whose ball of radius `2 R`
exhausts it, then `coveringNumber ε univ_X ≤ n ^ (k + 2)`.  This file lifts that
statement to a *family* `t : Set GHSpace`, in the exact language of the D12
compactness criterion `Poincare.D12.GeometricCompactness`:

* `exists_finset_ball_cover_card_le_of_coveringNumber_le` — the ENat/ENNReal
  bookkeeping: a bound `coveringNumber δ A ≤ K` (`K : ℕ`, `coveringNumber` valued
  in `ℕ∞`) yields an explicit finite cover by *open* balls of radius `ε > δ`
  (`≤` versus `<`, closed balls versus strict balls), via
  `Metric.exists_set_encard_eq_coveringNumber`.
* `coveringNumber_univ_le_of_uniformDoubling` — the family-level quantitative
  bound: a uniform doubling constant `n` on `t` plus a uniform scale bound
  (`univ ⊆ closedBall y (2 R)`) bounds `coveringNumber δ univ` by the explicit
  constant `n ^ (k + 2)` whenever `R / 2 ^ k ≤ δ`, for every member of `t`.
* `uniformCovers_of_uniformDoubling` — the right-hand side of D12's
  `uniformCovers_of_totallyBounded`: a uniform diameter bound *and*, for every
  `ε > 0`, a uniform bound `K` on the number of open `ε`-balls covering any
  member of `t`.
* `uniformCovers_of_uniformDoubling_familyScale` — the same with a per-member
  scale `R_p`, uniformly bounded by `R`.
* `coveringNumber_univ_le_of_ghDist_lt_of_familyDoubling` — the family-level
  consumer of the round-3 pair-level GH-transfer theorem (which is *consumed*,
  not reproved).
* `totallyBounded_of_uniformDoubling`, `isCompact_of_uniformDoubling` — the
  direction check against `totallyBounded_iff_uniformCovers` /
  `isCompact_of_uniformCovers`.  The direction fed is
  uniform covers ⟹ totally bounded/compact: `TotallyBounded t` is never assumed.
-/
```

